# Task 3 – Understand Linux Permissions

## Check Current Permissions

```bash
ls -l devops.txt notes.txt script.sh
```

### Example Format

```text
-rw-r--r--  owner group  ... devops.txt
-rw-r--r--  owner group  ... notes.txt
-rw-r--r--  owner group  ... script.sh
```

### Permission Format

```text
-rwxrwxrwx
 │   │   │
 │   │   └── Others
 │   └────── Group
 └────────── Owner
```

| Permission    | Numeric Value |
| ------------- | ------------: |
| Read (`r`)    |             4 |
| Write (`w`)   |             2 |
| Execute (`x`) |             1 |

### Example

```text
rwx = 7
rw- = 6
r-x = 5
r-- = 4
```

### Observation

Initially:

* Owner has read and write permission.
* Group has read permission.
* Others have read permission.
* `script.sh` does not have execute permission yet.

