# Real-World DevOps Connection

File permissions are important when working with:

```text
Configuration files
        ↓
/etc/*.conf

Scripts
        ↓
*.sh

Application files
        ↓
/opt/app

Logs
        ↓
/var/log

Deployment directories
        ↓
/var/www
```

For example, a deployment script may need execute permission:

```bash
chmod +x deploy.sh
```

A configuration file may need to be restricted:

```bash
chmod 640 application.conf
```

And an application directory may need controlled ownership and permissions.

