# Troubleshooting Example

### Problem

A script returns:

```text
Permission denied
```

### Investigation

Check the permissions:

```bash
ls -l script.sh
```

Check ownership:

```bash
ls -l script.sh
```

Check the current user:

```bash
whoami
```

If the script does not have execute permission:

```bash
chmod +x script.sh
```

Then test again:

```bash
./script.sh
```

### Troubleshooting Flow

```text
Permission Denied
       ↓
Check user
       ↓
Check ownership
       ↓
Check permissions
       ↓
Correct permissions/ownership
       ↓
Test again
```

